dreamer@uxa.cso.uiuc.edu (Andrew Trapp) writes:
> I would like to offer some of my observations now that I've played the newer 
> 3.1.1.  First, to all those people who say it's easier than 3.0j:  What the 
> HELL are you talking about??!?!  In 3.1.1 I _rarely_ get past level 4, or
> level 1 of the Gnomish Mines.  Damn monsters keep teaming up on me, wearing 
> me down.

The Mines are dangerous.  Don't go down them until you're well
armed and armored, and at experience level 6 at least.

> Second, what's the deal with the food?  I'm eating every edible corpse I
> kill and I'm still having to pray because I'm fainting from lack of food.
> In 3.0j starvation was never a problem, even in the earlier levels.

When you're Burdened or Stressed, you burn up food a lot faster.

> Thirdly:  The new weight system S U X !!!  If I accumulate any decent amount
> of possessions, my character moves slower.  When you're surrounded by hordes
> of rothes or hill orcs (I'm talking beginning levels here), the last thing
> you want is to find out to your suprise and your character's demise that all
> of a sudden, they get an _extra_ attack.  A burdened or stressed character
> now has to have the fast attribute _just_to_break_even_.  T'aint fair, I tell
> ya.

You can carry a greater number of possessions normally than you could
in 3.0, but in 3.1 the game will let you overburden yourself well
beyond that point.

There are messages warning you when you become overburdened, and it's
right there on the status line next to your hunger status; if you're
surprised to discover you've slowed down, you're not paying attention.

Turning on the "pickup" option often led to unintentionally
overburdening yourself when fighting hordes, however.  One step on a
pile of orcish helmets and chain mail could do you in.  In 3.1.2, the
"pickup" option has become "autopickup" and "pickup_types:", allowing
you to specify that what types of objects to pick up automatically
(ex. "pickup_types:$)?!+/"), and it will prompt you when you're
burdened.

> I also miss being able to easily rob shops blind.  I always ditched my pet
> on level 1 (preferably locked in a closet).  Now I have to put up with their
> stealing XP and corpses from me if I want to rob a shop.  I suppose this
> gripe I could learn to live with, but the game just isn't as fun.  (Tips on
> robbing shops early in the game would be much appreciated!  ;-)

It seems every version, the shopkeepers get a little smarter.  But the
oldest ways still work.  It's as easy as it ever was to grab a load of
stuff and teleport out.  Digging out is riskier and temporary, but
it still works too.

> On the plus side, I like the addition of more items, monsters, and special
> levels.  The line-of-sight thingy is also fairly nice, except I don't see
> why a monster should no longer be visible to me as it steps into a corridor
> coming towards me.

Corridors are dark.  If you have different symbols for light and dark
corridors, set the "lit_corridor" option to see the difference.


